From ef743269bed952597b3b84e0e7c8305a672d26bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] x86/mic: KNC platform code and the SFI firmware tables

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6:
 - intelmic.c: the x86_init/x86_platform hooks for the card
   (x86_mic_early_setup() from x86_64_start_kernel(), SBOX-based
   CPU/TSC calibration, wallclock, SMPT for host
   memory access, ISR setup, crash path), mic_etc.c: the ETC (elapsed
   time counter) clocksource used when the TSC is unstable across
   cpufreq changes, mic_v30_stubs.c; the SBOX ICR doorbell interrupts
   as their own irq_chip in io_apic.c (arch_setup_sbox_irqs).
 - The KNC bootstrap hands the CPU and IOAPIC tables to the kernel as
   SFI tables (CPUS/APIC); arch/x86/platform/sfi parses them and fills
   the KNC IOAPIC pin table.

Adaptations for 6.18:
 - Commit 4590d98f5a4f ("sfi: Remove framework for deprecated
   firmware") deleted SFI in 5.12; the 5.10 drivers/sfi core, headers
   and arch/x86/platform/sfi are carried here (the intel-mid users
   stay gone), with sfi_init_late() in init/main.c switching the
   tables from early_ioremap to ioremap (else check_early_ioremap_leak
   warns and late table access is wrong).
 - 6.9 topology: topology_register_apic() instead of
   generic_processor_info(); the SFI hook runs before
   x86_init.mpparse.parse_smp_cfg().
 - setup_arch() calls the calibrate hooks from
   simple_udelay_calibration() before ioremap() works (4.12):
   intel_mic_calibrate_tsc() returns 0 until the slab is up and
   tsc_init() asks again later.
 - Latent MPSS bugs fixed on the way: intel_mic_{get,set}_wallclock
   never filled the timespec (pre-3.9 prototypes), mic_setup_isr()
   was a void late_initcall.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
